          "topic": "Colligative properties and molar mass",
          "content_type": "explanation",
          "text": "Colligative properties depend on the number of dissolved solute particles relative to solvent particles, rather than the solute's chemical identity in the ideal dilute model. Examples include relative lowering of vapour pressure, boiling-point elevation, freezing-point depression, and osmotic pressure. Dissociation or association can change the effective particle count.",
