          "content_type": "worked_example",
          "text": "For a dilute solution with molality 0.20 mol/kg and water Kf = 1.86 K kg/mol, a non-electrolyte gives ΔTf = Kf m = 1.86 × 0.20 = 0.372 K. The solution's freezing point is about 0.372 °C below pure water's freezing point.",
