          "text": "A galvanic cell converts energy from a spontaneous redox reaction into electrical energy. Oxidation occurs at the anode and reduction at the cathode. Under standard conditions, E°cell = E°cathode - E°anode when tabulated reduction potentials are used; a positive value indicates spontaneity for the cell reaction as written under those conditions.",
