          "concept_id": "chem-12-chemical-kinetics-rate-law",
          "subject": "Chemistry",
          "class": 12,
          "chapter": "Chemical Kinetics",
          "topic": "Rate laws and reaction order",
          "content_type": "worked_example",
          "text": "If rate = k[A]^2[B], doubling [A] at fixed [B] multiplies the rate by 2^2 = 4. Doubling [B] at fixed [A] multiplies it by 2. The overall order is 2 + 1 = 3.",
