          "topic": "Nernst equation and concentration effects",
          "content_type": "explanation",
          "text": "The Nernst equation relates cell potential to concentrations and temperature. At 298 K, E = E° − (0.0591/n)log₁₀Q for a reaction involving n electrons. Q is built from activities (often approximated by concentrations) of products over reactants; pure solids and liquids are omitted.",
